<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
                            xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                            xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions"
                            revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0">
  <displayName>Claude Desktop</displayName>
  <description>Claude Desktop policy settings</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <!-- Categories -->
      <string id="Cat_ClaudeDesktop">Claude Desktop</string>
      <string id="Cat_ClaudeCode">Claude Code</string>
      <string id="Cat_Cowork">Cowork</string>
      <string id="Cat_Extensions">Extensions and MCP</string>
      <string id="Cat_SignIn">Sign-in</string>
      <string id="Cat_Updates">Updates</string>

      <!-- Supported on -->
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ClaudeDesktop">Claude Desktop for Windows</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ClaudeDesktop_1_25927">Claude Desktop for Windows 1.25927.0 or later</string>

      <!-- Claude Code -->
      <string id="isClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled">Allow Claude Code</string>
      <string id="isClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled_Explain">Controls whether users can access Claude Code in the Claude Desktop app.

If you enable or do not configure this policy setting, Claude Code is available in Claude Desktop. This is the default.

If you disable this policy setting, users cannot access Claude Code in Claude Desktop.

This policy setting applies only to Claude Desktop. The Claude Code CLI and IDE extensions are configured separately through Claude Code managed settings (HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\ClaudeCode).

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled (REG_DWORD; 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <string id="effortLevel">Default effort level</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_Explain">Sets the default effort level for Claude Code sessions in Claude Desktop.

If you enable this policy setting, the selected effort level is applied at the start of every Claude Code session, even if the user chose a different level from the effort picker in an earlier session. Available levels are low, medium, high, xhigh, and max.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, no managed default is applied.

This policy setting does not apply to Cowork sessions.

Requires Claude Desktop 1.25927.0 or later.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\effortLevel (REG_SZ)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_low">Low</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_medium">Medium</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_high">High</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_xhigh">Extra high</string>
      <string id="effortLevel_max">Max</string>

      <!-- Cowork -->
      <string id="secureVmFeaturesEnabled">Allow Cowork</string>
      <string id="secureVmFeaturesEnabled_Explain">Controls whether users can access Cowork in the Claude Desktop app.

If you enable or do not configure this policy setting, Cowork is available. This is the default.

If you disable this policy setting, users cannot access Cowork.

To keep Cowork available but limit which folders users can work in, use the "Allowed workspace folders" policy setting.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\secureVmFeaturesEnabled (REG_DWORD; 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <string id="allowedWorkspaceFolders">Allowed workspace folders</string>
      <string id="allowedWorkspaceFolders_Explain">Limits which folders users can mount into Cowork.

If you enable this policy setting, users can mount only the folders you list. Enter the folders as a single-line JSON array of paths, escaping each backslash:

["C:\\Projects","D:\\Shared"]

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, users can mount any folder. This is the default.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\allowedWorkspaceFolders (REG_SZ; JSON array)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <!-- Extensions and MCP -->
      <string id="isDesktopExtensionEnabled">Allow desktop extensions</string>
      <string id="isDesktopExtensionEnabled_Explain">Controls whether users can install and use desktop extensions in Claude Desktop.

If you enable or do not configure this policy setting, desktop extensions are allowed. This is the default.

If you disable this policy setting, desktop extensions are blocked.

Note: This policy setting overrides the desktop extension allowlist. If your organization uses the allowlist, do not disable this policy setting.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isDesktopExtensionEnabled (REG_DWORD; 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <string id="isDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled">Allow extension directory</string>
      <string id="isDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled_Explain">Controls whether users can browse and install extensions from the desktop extension directory in Claude Desktop.

If you enable or do not configure this policy setting, the extension directory is available. This is the default.

If you disable this policy setting, users cannot access the extension directory.

Note: The desktop extension allowlist populates available extensions through the directory. If your organization uses the allowlist, do not disable this policy setting.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled (REG_DWORD; 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <string id="isLocalDevMcpEnabled">Allow local MCP servers</string>
      <string id="isLocalDevMcpEnabled_Explain">Controls whether users can add and run local MCP servers in Claude Desktop.

If you enable or do not configure this policy setting, local MCP servers are allowed. This is the default.

If you disable this policy setting, local MCP servers are blocked.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isLocalDevMcpEnabled (REG_DWORD; 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <!-- Sign-in -->
      <string id="forceLoginOrgUUID">Restrict sign-in to organizations</string>
      <string id="forceLoginOrgUUID_Explain">Requires users to sign in to Claude Desktop with an account that belongs to one of your Claude organizations.

If you enable this policy setting, enter either:

- One organization UUID. Sign-in is restricted to that organization, and it is pre-selected on the sign-in screen.
  00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

- A single-line JSON array of organization UUIDs. Sign-in is allowed for any listed organization; none is pre-selected.
  ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"]

Sign-in fails for accounts that are not members of a listed organization.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, users can sign in with any account.

Claude Desktop reads this value at launch. Quit and reopen the app after a change.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\forceLoginOrgUUID (REG_SZ; a JSON array is stored as one string, not REG_MULTI_SZ)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <!-- Updates -->
      <string id="disableAutoUpdates">Disable automatic updates</string>
      <string id="disableAutoUpdates_Explain">Controls whether Claude Desktop updates itself automatically.

If you enable this policy setting, automatic updates are turned off. Use this when your software deployment tool manages Claude Desktop versions.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, automatic updates are turned on. This is the default, and lets Claude Desktop keep itself current after a one-time provisioned install.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\disableAutoUpdates (REG_DWORD; 1 = updates off, 0 = updates on)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>

      <string id="autoUpdaterEnforcementHours">Update restart deadline</string>
      <string id="autoUpdaterEnforcementHours_Explain">Sets how long Claude Desktop waits after an update is prepared before it restarts to apply the update.

If you enable this policy setting, enter a deadline from 1 to 72 hours. When the deadline passes, Claude Desktop restarts automatically to apply the prepared update.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the deadline is 72 hours. This is the default.

Registry value: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\autoUpdaterEnforcementHours (REG_DWORD; 1-72)

For more information, see https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12622667</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="effortLevel">
        <dropdownList refId="effortLevel" defaultItem="2" noSort="true">Effort level:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="allowedWorkspaceFolders">
        <textBox refId="allowedWorkspaceFolders">
          <label>Folders (JSON array):</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="forceLoginOrgUUID">
        <textBox refId="forceLoginOrgUUID">
          <label>Organization UUID or JSON array:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="autoUpdaterEnforcementHours">
        <decimalTextBox refId="autoUpdaterEnforcementHours" defaultValue="72" spinStep="1">Hours (1-72):</decimalTextBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
